From 3d2bde47e865fcd62f500afd147c110a719020e3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Francesco Riosa <me@francesco-riosa.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 20:22:13 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix(parser): make `declare -f` of a here-document parseable
 and idempotent
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Serializing a function whose body contains a here-document produced
output that neither bash nor brush could re-parse, and that grew on every
round-trip.

- Here-document bodies are deferred. `IoRedirect`'s `Display` now emits
  only `[fd]<<[-]<tag>` on the command line and queues the body;
  `CompoundList::fmt_items` flushes the queue at the end of the line, at
  column 0, in place of the item's `;` separator -- matching how a shell
  prints a command (bash's `deferred_heredocs` in `print_cmd.c`).
  Previously the body was written inline, indented by the enclosing
  block, and ahead of any later redirection on the same command.

- `indenter` is replaced by a local `ShellIndent` (dropping the
  dependency) that additionally leaves a line at column 0 when its
  starting newline was emitted inside a verbatim span -- a deferred
  here-doc body, or the interior of a multi-line word (`local x='…\n…'`).
  A shell prints words verbatim; re-indenting their interior lines made
  `declare -f` non-idempotent (each round-trip added a level).

- Process substitution renders its inner list directly -- `>(list)` --
  not via `SubshellCommand`'s own parentheses (`>(( list ))`, which
  compounded).

- `|` and file-descriptor-duplication (`>&1`, `<&-`) spacing now match a
  shell's output (`a | b`, not `a |b`; `2>&1`, not `2>& 1`).

Adds compat cases for a here-document, a process substitution, a
multi-line quoted string, and an explicit `declare -f` idempotency check.
